A||||14||ponya||Seat covers||||5||
Z||000000||ponya||08-30-2000||08:31 PM||||I know that Mr. Mike's is the place to go to get leather seat covers. Is there anyone like Mr. Mike that sells fabric seat covers? I need seat covers, just don't have that much money to invest in leather seats. Any info appreciated.      Bob||||reg||5
Z||000001||Boomtastic||08-30-2000||08:43 PM||||I was looking for seat covers for my Formula. The only place I found that looked "OEM" was a local automotive upholstery shop near me in MA. Eventually I broke down and bought the Mr Mikes leather kit. I highly recommend that you continue to save and get this kit - it's beyond belief, both in looks and in comfort!!||||reg||14
Z||000002||rockcrawl||08-30-2000||09:39 PM||||The Fiero store has OEM style fabric covers, but the price is very close to that of leather. I wanted to re-cover the seats in one of my cars and keep the original look, but now I can't decide. A local upholstry shop quoted me $400 to do two seats in fabric.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'86 GT 3800 (for sale)<BR>'87 GT (noisey 2.8)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||08-31-2000||12:04 AM||||Although I've never had Mr. Mikes seat covers, I'd still have to say that that's the way to go.  I've been to some upholsterererers, too, and they want as much to do cloth as Mr. Mikes want's for leather.  I've never been a fan of leather (cold in the winter and hot in the summer), but that's probably what I'll end up doing.  Just trying to find a stock seat cover in the meantime.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||08-31-2000||02:17 AM||||Monkeyman, Mr. Mike's seats now have a seat heater option for winter! My seats don't get that hot in the summer and I usually have the sunroof off the car. (I know you don't open yours  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  )<BR>By far the best route is to get the leather. The only way to do it cheaper is to make your own. Most shops will charge $400 and up for cloth.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||08-31-2000||11:01 AM||||Oreif--I just found out about that heater option last time I spoke with Mr. Mike (few weeks ago).  Seems like that's just for the bottom of the seat, though.  I still think the seat back would be a little chilly, but by the time I'm ready to spend that kind of money on covers, I will probably have already installed a remote start so it won't matter.  Mr. Mikes is still my 1st choice.   (Although I'm not very happy with him right now.  I asked him to send me some leather samples about 3 weeks ago.  I called him about a week and a half ago inquiring about them.  Still haven't received them. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">)||||reg||1
Z||000006||ChadMan||08-31-2000||11:07 AM||||I got a whole new driver's seat for my 88 Coupe from Kick Hill Farm for $100.  Not cheap, but half the price of Mr. Mike's and I didn't want leather in an un-air-conditioned car anyway.<P>I don't think you'll find a cheaper option if you want stock fabric on your seats, unless you get lucky and see somebody selling factory seat covers in your color/model/year on eBay.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Oreif||08-31-2000||11:08 AM||||Monkeyman, If you go to Mr Mike's site you'll see it covers the bottom and the back. <BR> <A HREF="http://www.mrmikes.com" TARGET=_blank>www.mrmikes.com</A><P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/heatedseatslg.jpg"> <P><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 08-31-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Monkeyman||08-31-2000||01:49 PM||||My bad.  It sure does.  I'll probably go with Mr. Mikes once I get to that stage, but like I said, I'm a little frustrated with him right now.  I know he's a nice guy.  I've spoken with him before and have received lots of good advice/directions, etc, but he still never sent me the samples.  Maybe I'll give him a call and try to get it straightened out.||||reg||1
Z||000009||87ECO5||08-31-2000||02:18 PM||||Everyone talks about replacing their seat covers with the leather covers.  And I'm assuming it's mainly because the cloth covers have that common bolster wear.<P>But, has anyone discussed how to prevent that with the new covers?  I'm sure it took years to wear through the cloth but won't the leather begin showing wear (scrapes, scratches, etc.) long before the cloth would?||||reg||5
Z||000010||HugGRRRFiero||08-31-2000||02:36 PM||||I've seen wear on the "cheeks" of leather Indy seats.  The piping that runs along that seam takes a beating too.  So wear is probably a problem with leathers as well.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">  <BR>  <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||mrfixit58||08-31-2000||02:54 PM||||Most of us (at least more than will admit it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ) have bigger butts then the car was intended to accomodate. I can't think of anything short of teflon that would stop the wear on the bolsters. <P>There is one option that I've seen on another type of car that would help but I don't think that it would be practicle in a Fiero... swivel bucket seats! :razz:<P>I took a pair out of a 70's vintage Monte Carlo and adapted them to work (partially) in my old 1970 Chevy LUV truck (Don't laugh, I also installed a SBC, TH350, and a 8-bolt rear-end). Like these hot rod Fieros... I suprised more than one Camaro owner.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><P>Anyway, the thing I do to control the wear is to be very careful entering and leaving the car. Try to sit down without sliding down the bolsters. As it tuns out, it's also better for my back (no old jokes, please).<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000012||Gold-86SE||08-31-2000||03:18 PM||||<BR>I do this to prevent further wear on the edge of the seat.<P>1) Slide it all the way back before leaving the Fiero<P>2) Don't wear any Docker style pants that have buttonable rear pockets, or if you do, undo the button before entering the car.<P>It takes awhile to get use to doing both of these things, but it saves wear on the seat.<P>Just my $0.02<BR><P>------------------<BR>Gold-86SE (Fiero Collector)||||reg||1
Z||000013||Phil||08-31-2000||04:42 PM||||Pisa also has leather seats||||reg||1
Z||000014||Monkeyman||09-01-2000||12:10 AM||||Just a quick note about my frustration with Mr. Mike---He has redeemed himself.  I just got home from work to find an envelope with the samples in it.  Leather, carpet and headliner samples.  Better late than never.  ||||reg||1
